{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjJ3AfcgXgYkYstojGNZgt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# R25 — Backend review — Phase 3 memory graph storage\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** Review for Phase 3\n4\t**Type:** review\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** T19, T20, T21, T22, T23, T24\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-3-memory-graph-storage)\n8\t\n9\t## Purpose\n10\t\n11\tThis review certifies that the Phase 3 memory graph substrate satisfies every spec invariant before retrieval (Phase 4) starts depending on it. It confirms: the schema covers all 13 memory classes (including `CounterMemory` as a first-class record); links, evidence, accesses, and scores are first-class tables; stream classification and scope enforcement deny-by-default work as specified; the legacy migration imports cleanly and idempotently; CRUD plus the full verification-status state machine emits the right events; contradiction, supersession, stale state, and replay all behave correctly. The verdict gates R26 (contract gate) and Phase 4.\n12\t\n13\t## Inputs to read\n14\t\n15\t- Every artifact from T19–T24:\n16\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/mod.rs`, `classes.rs`, `schema.sql`\n17\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/links.rs`, `evidence.rs`, `accesses.rs`, `scores.rs`, `links_tests.rs`\n18\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/streams.rs`, `scope.rs`, `scope_tests.rs`\n19\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/migration.rs`, `migration_tests.rs`\n20\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/store.rs`, `transitions.rs`, `store_tests.rs`\n21\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/contradiction_tests.rs`, `supersession_tests.rs`, `replay_tests.rs`\n22\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md`\n23\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-migration-guide.md`\n24\t- Spec sections claimed satisfied:\n25\t  - §Memory Graph (classes including CounterMemory, required fields, link types)\n26\t  - §ViLoMem (typed streams)\n27\t  - §Storage Design (memories, memory_links, memory_evidence, memory_accesses, memory_scores, indexes)\n28\t  - §Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage (Deliverables + DoD)\n29\t  - §Risks \"Scope Leakage\" and the deny-by-default control\n30\t- Standards relevant to this phase: Cadres coding standard §Schema / model parity, §Error handling, §Naming, §No broken windows; Lattice CLAUDE.md on Markdown heading references.\n31\t\n32\t## Review procedure\n33\t\n34\t1. Confirm `MemoryClass` enumerates all 13 spec variants and `CounterMemory` is present.\n35\t2. Confirm `MemoryRecord` has one field per spec-required attribute; cross-check the schema column inventory against the spec list.\n36\t3. Confirm the four first-class tables exist (`memory_links`, `memory_evidence`, `memory_accesses`, `memory_scores`) with the columns and indexes from spec §Storage Design.\n37\t4. Confirm `MemoryLinkType` enumerates all 11 spec variants; exhaustive `match` is used at write/read sites.\n38\t5. Confirm `MemoryStream` enumerates the seven streams and `classify_stream` is total over `MemoryClass`.\n39\t6. Confirm `ScopeFilter` is required on every read API (compile-time enforcement preferred; runtime `Underspecified` if not); confirm cross-scope leakage negative tests exist and pass.\n40\t7. Confirm the migration importer is idempotent, dry-runnable, restartable, and that every legacy column has a documented destination in the migration-guide column-mapping table.\n41\t8. Confirm the verification-status state machine matches the spec list and that disallowed transitions return typed errors.\n42\t9. Confirm contradiction tests exercise both the `Contradicts` link path AND the `CounterMemory` first-class-record path, and that the two are observably distinct (CounterMemory has its own id, evidence, scope, and verification status).\n43\t10. Confirm supersession chains preserve historical lookup and reject cycles.\n44\t11. Confirm replay tests show byte-equivalence between full replay and snapshot + tail, and that corruption returns a typed error without silent recovery.\n45\t12. Run the verification commands from tasks.json for T19–T24 from the repo root.\n46\t13. Audit for coding-standard regressions: file lengths, function lengths, error-swallowing, raw-SQL interpolation, missing tracing on transitions.\n47\t\n48\t## Required sections in the review output file\n49\t\n50\t`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` with these mandatory headings:\n51\t\n52\t- `## Spec alignment` — table mapping each Phase 3 deliverable + DoD line to the artifact that satisfies it.\n53\t- `## Coding-standard alignment` — file-length, function-length, error-handling, schema-parity, SQL-binding, tracing audit results.\n54\t- `## CounterMemory coverage` — explicit confirmation that `CounterMemory` is a first-class class (not just a link), with citations to the test names that prove it carries its own evidence, scope, verification status, and can itself be superseded or invalidated.\n55\t- `## Findings` — every defect, missing artifact, or weak test, each with a severity (blocker / major / minor) and the task that owns the fix.\n56\t- `## Verdict` — `APPROVED` / `APPROVED WITH FOLLOW-UPS` / `REJECTED`. A `REJECTED` verdict blocks R26 from starting.\n57\t\n58\t## Verification\n59\t\n60\t- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — review file exists.\n61\t- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — spec-alignment section present.\n62\t- `grep -q '## CounterMemory coverage' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — CounterMemory section present per Phase 3 DoD.\n63\t- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — verdict recorded.\n64\t\n65\t## Definition of done\n66\t\n67\t- [ ] Review markdown file exists.\n68\t- [ ] Every required section present with concrete content (no placeholder text).\n69\t- [ ] Contract tests added (R26 only) and passing — not applicable to R25.\n70\t- [ ] Verdict declared.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c80d671-1437-429b-9e3a-231a1f740b4b","uuid":"14c92840-b2a6-4270-9468-546c022f7a25","timestamp":"2026-05-17T07:18:28.116Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R25.md","content":"# R25 — Backend review — Phase 3 memory graph storage\n\n**Phase:** Review for Phase 3\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T19, T20, T21, T22, T23, T24\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-3-memory-graph-storage)\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis review certifies that the Phase 3 memory graph substrate satisfies every spec invariant before retrieval (Phase 4) starts depending on it. It confirms: the schema covers all 13 memory classes (including `CounterMemory` as a first-class record); links, evidence, accesses, and scores are first-class tables; stream classification and scope enforcement deny-by-default work as specified; the legacy migration imports cleanly and idempotently; CRUD plus the full verification-status state machine emits the right events; contradiction, supersession, stale state, and replay all behave correctly. The verdict gates R26 (contract gate) and Phase 4.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact from T19–T24:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/mod.rs`, `classes.rs`, `schema.sql`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/links.rs`, `evidence.rs`, `accesses.rs`, `scores.rs`, `links_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/streams.rs`, `scope.rs`, `scope_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/migration.rs`, `migration_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/store.rs`, `transitions.rs`, `store_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/contradiction_tests.rs`, `supersession_tests.rs`, `replay_tests.rs`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-migration-guide.md`\n- Spec sections claimed satisfied:\n  - §Memory Graph (classes including CounterMemory, required fields, link types)\n  - §ViLoMem (typed streams)\n  - §Storage Design (memories, memory_links, memory_evidence, memory_accesses, memory_scores, indexes)\n  - §Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage (Deliverables + DoD)\n  - §Risks \"Scope Leakage\" and the deny-by-default control\n- Standards relevant to this phase: Cadres coding standard §Schema / model parity, §Error handling, §Naming, §No broken windows; Lattice CLAUDE.md on Markdown heading references.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Confirm `MemoryClass` enumerates all 13 spec variants and `CounterMemory` is present.\n2. Confirm `MemoryRecord` has one field per spec-required attribute; cross-check the schema column inventory against the spec list.\n3. Confirm the four first-class tables exist (`memory_links`, `memory_evidence`, `memory_accesses`, `memory_scores`) with the columns and indexes from spec §Storage Design.\n4. Confirm `MemoryLinkType` enumerates all 11 spec variants; exhaustive `match` is used at write/read sites.\n5. Confirm `MemoryStream` enumerates the seven streams and `classify_stream` is total over `MemoryClass`.\n6. Confirm `ScopeFilter` is required on every read API (compile-time enforcement preferred; runtime `Underspecified` if not); confirm cross-scope leakage negative tests exist and pass.\n7. Confirm the migration importer is idempotent, dry-runnable, restartable, and that every legacy column has a documented destination in the migration-guide column-mapping table.\n8. Confirm the verification-status state machine matches the spec list and that disallowed transitions return typed errors.\n9. Confirm contradiction tests exercise both the `Contradicts` link path AND the `CounterMemory` first-class-record path, and that the two are observably distinct (CounterMemory has its own id, evidence, scope, and verification status).\n10. Confirm supersession chains preserve historical lookup and reject cycles.\n11. Confirm replay tests show byte-equivalence between full replay and snapshot + tail, and that corruption returns a typed error without silent recovery.\n12. Run the verification commands from tasks.json for T19–T24 from the repo root.\n13. Audit for coding-standard regressions: file lengths, function lengths, error-swallowing, raw-SQL interpolation, missing tracing on transitions.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\n`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` with these mandatory headings:\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — table mapping each Phase 3 deliverable + DoD line to the artifact that satisfies it.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — file-length, function-length, error-handling, schema-parity, SQL-binding, tracing audit results.\n- `## CounterMemory coverage` — explicit confirmation that `CounterMemory` is a first-class class (not just a link), with citations to the test names that prove it carries its own evidence, scope, verification status, and can itself be superseded or invalidated.\n- `## Findings` — every defect, missing artifact, or weak test, each with a severity (blocker / major / minor) and the task that owns the fix.\n- `## Verdict` — `APPROVED` / `APPROVED WITH FOLLOW-UPS` / `REJECTED`. A `REJECTED` verdict blocks R26 from starting.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — review file exists.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — spec-alignment section present.\n- `grep -q '## CounterMemory coverage' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — CounterMemory section present per Phase 3 DoD.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R25-memory-graph.md` — verdict recorded.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists.\n- [ ] Every required section present with concrete content (no placeholder text).\n- [ ] Contract tests added (R26 only) and passing — not applicable to R25.\n- [ ] Verdict declared.\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
